      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 28,
      "padding": [
        236,
        260,
        354,
        236
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "eX0KU",
          "name": "s1b_hdr",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "alignItems": "center",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "xadEV",
              "name": "s1b_lab",
              "fill": "#B8860B",
              "content": "Session 1",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 75,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tht5N",
              "name": "s1b_ttl",
              "fill": "#2C2420",
              "content": "The Heart of Worship (3)",
              "textAlign": "center",
              "fontFamily": "Playfair Display",
              "fontSize": 100,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "fontStyle": "italic"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "wdMRN",
          "name": "s1b_3t",
          "fill": "#2C2420",
          "content": "A Steady Worship Life Needs 3 Things",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 75,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "omQXa",
          "name": "s1b_3box",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 22,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "BBhJ5",
              "name": "box1",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "stroke": {
                "thickness": 1,
                "fill": "#E5DDD2"
              },
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "padding": [
                14,
                20
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "WCgdE",
                  "name": "box1t",
                  "fill": "#B8860B",
                  "content": "The Word of God",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "9mIa1",
                  "name": "box1d",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The Word of God is essential. Without it, believers will not know what is right or wrong and may be deceived by false teaching. Christians should read the Bible every day, love the Word, and let it take deep root in their lives.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Gd7py",
              "name": "box2",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "stroke": {
                "thickness": 1,
                "fill": "#E5DDD2"
              },
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "padding": [
                14,
                20
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "azvfu",
                  "name": "box2t",
                  "fill": "#B8860B",
                  "content": "Prayer",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "1C8vv",
                  "name": "box2d",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Prayer has power to change everything. Human ability can change only some things, but prayer can bring remarkable change. Keep praying and do not lose heart. If necessary, fast and pray. Revival is born from praying knees.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "cMbXL",
              "name": "box3",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "stroke": {
                "thickness": 1,
                "fill": "#E5DDD2"
              },
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "padding": [
                14,
                20
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "827ac",
                  "name": "box3t",
                  "fill": "#B8860B",
                  "content": "Worship (Through Song)",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "U7rou",
                  "name": "box3d",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Scripture supports the use of song and music. The Bible speaks many times about praising God with instruments, especially in Psalm 150, which calls everything that has breath to praise the Lord.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "w6fQz",
          "layoutPosition": "absolute",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 3400,
          "name": "l8",
          "fill": "#6B5D52",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 2480,
          "content": "8",
          "textAlign": "center",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 42,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "AbfQL",
      "x": 20640,
      "y": 5000,
      "name": "copy4",
      "width": 2480,
      "height": 3508,
      "fill": "#FFFFFF",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": [
        236,
        260,
        354,
        236
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "GtRui",
          "name": "hdrB",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "alignItems": "center",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vaXwb",
              "name": "labB",
              "fill": "#B8860B",
              "content": "Session 1",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 75,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "zWv50",
              "name": "ttlB",
              "fill": "#2C2420",
              "content": "The Heart of Worship (4)",
              "textAlign": "center",
              "fontFamily": "Playfair Display",
              "fontSize": 100,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "fontStyle": "italic"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "aYBg2",
          "name": "sec3",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "1xUUC",
              "name": "sec3t",
              "fill": "#2C2420",
              "content": "3. The Power of Worship (What Worship Does)",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 75,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "l6eo5",
              "name": "sec3b",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 30,
              "padding": [
                0,
                0,
                0,
                16
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "OrC7w",
                  "name": "sec3p1",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Worship songs are different from ordinary songs. Ordinary songs may sound beautiful, but worship songs carry power to build and transform spiritual life. As we listen to and sing worship songs again and again, the truths of God sink deep into our hearts and change our lives.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "iXksG",
                  "name": "sec3p2a",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "In times of crisis, sometimes we cannot read Scripture or even find words to pray. Yet when worship music is played, we encounter God again and receive strength, healing, and comfort through the song. Worship is not only something we do, but something that changes us.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xb5s7",
                  "name": "sec3p2",
                  "fill": "#2C2420",
                  "content": "When we worship:",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "nyVf7",
                  "name": "sec3l1",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "•  We come to know God more\n•  We love God more\n•  We hear His voice more clearly\n•  We experience God's presence\n•  We grow and become steady in faith",
                  "lineHeight": 1.7,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hQH0t",
                  "name": "sec3p3",
                  "fill": "#B8860B",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Worship also leads to healing, deliverance, restoration, and peace.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 75,
                  "fontWeight": "500"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JrbsM",
                  "name": "sec3p4",
                  "fill": "#6B5D52",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Many times, worship songs can touch a person's heart before they even understand the sermon.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
